# Vestige Deterministic Guardrails

Before modifying any source file, follow these deterministic checks using the local Vestige MCP tools:

1. Start every session by calling `session(action="start")` to load pinned engineering invariants and active intentions from the local Strata ledger.
2. Before editing a high-churn or previously reverted file, call `recall` or `causal_walk(action="fence", ...)` to check Chesterton's Fence guards and prior failure receipts so reverted bugs are never re-introduced.
3. If a test fails or a build breaks, call `causal_walk` pointed at the failing symbol before guessing at a fix.
4. Anchor every verified architectural decision or bug resolution back into Strata with `remember(action="save", ...)` and supersede invalidated facts via `curate`.
5. Respect any active `vestige lease` scope boundaries and never attempt to bypass an Operator guard stop.
